1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,661
Every year, a wall of wildebeest

2
00:00:02,661 --> 00:00:04,547
hurls itself into a river

3
00:00:04,547 --> 00:00:06,417
full of crocodiles.

4
00:00:06,517 --> 00:00:09,235
Why would any animal take that risk?

5
00:00:09,335 --> 00:00:10,953
The answer is grass.

6
00:00:10,953 --> 00:00:13,131
Rain falls at different times

7
00:00:13,131 --> 00:00:16,181
across the plains, and fresh shoots follow,

8
00:00:16,181 --> 00:00:18,709
rich in protein and minerals.

9
00:00:18,809 --> 00:00:21,343
So the herds follow the rain,

10
00:00:21,343 --> 00:00:24,312
in a clockwise loop of about 800 km

11
00:00:24,312 --> 00:00:27,052
between Tanzania and Kenya.

12
00:00:27,152 --> 00:00:28,886
It begins in the south.

13
00:00:28,886 --> 00:00:31,457
Early in the year, up to 8,000 calves

14
00:00:31,457 --> 00:00:33,490
can be born in a single day,

15
00:00:33,490 --> 00:00:35,993
and they stand within minutes.

16
00:00:36,093 --> 00:00:37,899
As the plains dry out,

17
00:00:37,899 --> 00:00:40,478
zebra and gazelle march with them,

18
00:00:40,478 --> 00:00:42,155
west and then north,

19
00:00:42,155 --> 00:00:44,606
until they reach the Mara River,

20
00:00:44,606 --> 00:00:47,600
the only reliable dry-season water.

21
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:52,701
From around July, they cross.

22
00:00:52,701 --> 00:00:54,525
Thousands jump at once,

23
00:00:54,525 --> 00:00:56,887
and crocodiles wait below.

24
00:00:56,987 --> 00:00:59,882
Around 6,000 drown in an average year.

25
00:00:59,882 --> 00:01:01,725
But nothing is wasted.

26
00:01:01,725 --> 00:01:05,102
Their bones feed the river for ~7 years.

27
00:01:05,202 --> 00:01:07,956
For decades the herd was put

28
00:01:07,956 --> 00:01:09,657
at 1.3 million.

29
00:01:09,657 --> 00:01:13,059
In 2025, an AI count from satellites

30
00:01:13,059 --> 00:01:15,920
found fewer than 600,000.

31
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:18,532
Fences, farms and a shrinking river

32
00:01:18,532 --> 00:01:20,658
now press on the route.

33
00:01:20,758 --> 00:01:23,486
Keep the land open and the water flowing,

34
00:01:23,486 --> 00:01:26,100
and the great loop keeps turning.
